p({"class": "foam.core.reflow.Flow", "category": "DEMO", "name": "functionBlocks", "description": "Demo of the function command: a block whose returned value is read by later blocks under its name, instead of being parked on globalThis.", "version": 1, "script": "[{\"flowName\": \"title\", \"cmd\": \"h1 Function Blocks\"}, {\"flowName\": \"intro\", \"cmd\": \"markdown A **function** block runs like a script block, but keeps what its code returns as the block's value. Other blocks read that value by the block's name - in their own code, in a dao command, or in a reactive formula. That is the difference from a script block that parks its result on globalThis: a name is a dependency the Console can see, so the block appears in the dependency tree and the loader knows it has to finish first. Open each block below to read its code.\"}, {\"flowName\": \"regions\", \"cmd\": \"dao region\", \"value\": {\"class\": \"foam.core.reflow.DAOPrompt\", \"label\": \"All regions\", \"columns\": \"name,countryId,isoCode\"}}, {\"flowName\": \"canadaRows\", \"cmd\": \"function\", \"value\": {\"class\": \"foam.core.reflow.function.Function\", \"code\": \"// Read the DAO once. Whatever this returns is the block's value,\\n// and the blocks below read it as canadaRows.\\nvar rs = await regions.filteredDAO.select();\\nreturn rs.array.filter(r => r.countryId === 'CA');\\n\", \"autoRun\": true}, \"shown\": false}, {\"flowName\": \"canadaCount\", \"cmd\": \"function\", \"value\": {\"class\": \"foam.core.reflow.function.Function\", \"code\": \"// A function reading another function: no globalThis, no ordering guesswork.\\n// canadaRows ran to completion before this block started.\\nreturn canadaRows.length;\\n\", \"autoRun\": true}, \"shown\": false}, {\"flowName\": \"summary\", \"cmd\": \"markdown\", \"value\": {\"class\": \"foam.core.reflow.Markdown\", \"reactions_\": {\"markdown\": \"'**' + canadaCount + '** of those regions are Canadian, listed below.'\"}}}, {\"flowName\": \"canadaDAO\", \"cmd\": \"function\", \"value\": {\"class\": \"foam.core.reflow.function.Function\", \"code\": \"// Returning a DAO makes the block usable wherever a DAO is: the block below\\n// is a plain dao command reading this one by name. A block whose name ends\\n// in DAO is bound without the suffix too, so canada works as well.\\nvar dao = foam.dao.MDAO.create({ of: foam.core.auth.Region }, x);\\ncanadaRows.forEach(r => dao.put(r));\\nreturn dao;\\n\", \"autoRun\": true}, \"shown\": false}, {\"flowName\": \"canadaTable\", \"cmd\": \"dao(canadaDAO, 'Canadian regions')\", \"value\": {\"class\": \"foam.core.reflow.DAOPrompt\", \"label\": \"Canadian regions\", \"columns\": \"name,isoCode,code\"}}, {\"flowName\": \"outro\", \"cmd\": \"markdown Nothing above was handed over through globalThis. Select any block and the tree on the left lists the blocks that depend on it, because a reference to a function block is just its name in another block's code. A function block also warns when its code has no return at all - that is a script block, not a function - and it logs what came back, Array(12) or a class id, rather than dumping a whole DAO into the output.\"}]"})
